## 10. Package and Module Structure [DASH-PACKAGE]

### 10.1 Location [DASH-PACKAGE-LOC]

```
ux_composer/
  src/
    dashboard/
      __init__.py
      __main__.py          # Entry point: python -m composeio.dashboard
      app.py               # DashboardApp(ComposeApp) — lifecycle, YAML loading
      browser.py           # Browser mode UI (file picker + bus_storage list)
      layout.py            # Grid layout builder from YAML module/widget structure
      status_bar.py        # Connection status indicator
    composeio_renderers/   # Shared rendering layer (spec 11) — used by dashboard AND ComposeUX
      __init__.py
      context.py           # RendererContext dataclass
      factory.py           # RendererFactory registry
      base.py              # WidgetRenderer base class
      gauge.py             # GaugeRenderer
      button.py            # ButtonRenderer
      relay.py             # RelayRenderer
      coordinate.py        # CoordinateEntryRenderer
      bus_monitor.py       # BusMonitorRenderer
      tab.py               # TabRenderer
      placeholder.py       # PlaceholderRenderer
```

### 10.2 Entry Point [DASH-PACKAGE-ENTRY]

`__main__.py` parses CLI arguments, determines launch mode, and delegates to `DashboardApp`. The `DashboardApp` class is the ComposeApp subclass that orchestrates the lifecycle.

### 10.3 Dependencies [DASH-PACKAGE-DEPS]

| Dependency | Purpose | Version |
|------------|---------|---------|
| `customtkinter` | UI framework | >=5.0 |
| `composeio` | Bus library (ComposeApp, ComposeIOBus, transports) | local |
| `pyyaml` | YAML parsing | >=6.0 |
| `paho-mqtt` | MQTT transport (via composeio) | >=1.6 |
| `requests` | bus_storage HTTP queries (browser mode) | >=2.28 |

---

## 11. Compliance Requirements [DASH-COMPLIANCE]

A compliant Runtime Dashboard implementation MUST:

1. **[DASH-C1]** Load any valid `.compose.yaml` with top-level type `app` and render all built-in widget types (ButtonWidget, GaugeWidget, RelayWidget, CoordinateEntryWidget, BusMonitorWidget, TabWidget)
2. **[DASH-C2]** Connect to MQTT and display live namespace values within 500ms of state change on the bus
3. **[DASH-C3]** Interactive widgets (ButtonWidget, CoordinateEntryWidget) MUST publish state changes to the external bus when the user interacts
4. **[DASH-C4]** Support browser mode when launched without a YAML argument — file picker and (when reachable) bus_storage listing
5. **[DASH-C5]** Clean shutdown via `ComposeApp.stop()` — no orphaned MQTT connections, no leaked threads
6. **[DASH-C6]** Render unknown widget types as a visible placeholder showing type name and raw namespace value, not silently skip them
7. **[DASH-C7]** Respect the `_app/` default-deny boundary per [APP-C8] — no internal namespaces leak to external bus without explicit routing
8. **[DASH-C8]** Support `--no-connect` offline mode that renders layout without transport connection
9. **[DASH-C9]** Thread-safe rendering — MQTT callbacks MUST NOT directly modify CTk widgets; use `after()` scheduling
10. **[DASH-C10]** CLI `--broker` and `--port` MUST override YAML-declared transport configuration

A compliant implementation SHOULD:

11. **[DASH-S1]** Animate gauge needle transitions (smooth interpolation, not snap)
12. **[DASH-S2]** Display connection status indicator with reconnection state
13. **[DASH-S3]** Support multiple simultaneous transports (MQTT + UART)
14. **[DASH-S4]** Auto-reconnect on transport disconnect with exponential backoff
15. **[DASH-S5]** Support `design.target` window sizing from YAML metadata

